winexinput.sys,xinput1_3: Read the Xbox Bluetooth gamepad layout.

Without SDL, an Xbox Wireless Controller paired over Bluetooth reaches
winebus through IOHID as its raw HID device, and its report does not look like
the one Wine's two XInput readers assume. The right stick is on Z/Rz rather
than Rx/Ry, the triggers are on the Simulation page's Brake and Accelerator,
the buttons are numbered with gaps (A=1, B=2, X=4, Y=5, LB=7, RB=8, View=11,
Menu=12, LS=14, RS=15), and the Y axes grow downwards as HID's do. On Linux
SDL rewrites all of this before Wine sees it; protium's build has no SDL, and
CrossOver's own Xbox bus disables itself on macOS 15 and later.

Read as it stands, the right stick is missing, its movement appears on both
triggers (resting at 128), the real triggers do nothing, the bumpers read as
Back and Start, and X reads as Y. Measured on a 045e:0b13 (firmware
5.9.2709.0) under Wine 11.0 from crossover-sources-26.3.0; see
docs/controllers.md.

When a gamepad has Z and Rz, Brake and Accelerator, and no Rx or Ry, read
Z/Rz as the right stick and Brake/Accelerator as the triggers, renumber the
buttons, and take Y as HID gives it. A device without that shape is read
exactly as before.

